N2  - Abstract The stable isotopic composition of clay minerals, volcanic glass, and leaf waxes preserved in paleochannels of the northern Sierra Nevada (California, USA) shows higher than modern elevations in the Paleogene, yet this result remains debated due to difficulty reconciling the topography and geomorphology of the modern and ancient landscapes. Here, we present new leaf wax hydrogen isotope data (δ2HnC29) from individual fossil leaves preserved in Eocene–Oligocene alluvial gravels of the no
